a":"துஞ்சு","gloss":"sleep"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without sleeping"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பசலை","parts":[{"text":"பசலை","lemma":"பசலை","gloss":"pallor"}],"gloss":"pallor"},{"surface":"ஆகி","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"become"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having become"},{"surface":"விளிவது","parts":[{"text":"விளி","lemma":"விளி","gloss":"perish"},{"text":"வது","lemma":"வது","gloss":"nominalizing suffix"}],"gloss":"perishing"},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"கொல்","gloss":"particle of doubt"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"particle of wonder"}],"gloss":"is it indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெண்குருகு","parts":[{"text":"வெண்குருகு","lemma":"வெண்குருகு","gloss":"white heron"}],"gloss":"white heron"},{"surface":"நரலும்","parts":[{"text":"நரல்","lemma":"நரல்","gloss":"cry"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"crying"},{"surface":"தண்கமழ்","parts":[{"text":"தண்கமழ்","lemma":"தண்கமழ்","gloss":"cool and fragrant"}],"gloss":"cool and fragrant"},{"surface":"கானல்","parts":[{"text":"கானல்","lemma":"கானல்","gloss":"seashore grove"}],"gloss":"seashore grove"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூமலி","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"பூ","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"மலி","lemma":"மலி","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"flower-rich"},{"surface":"பொதும்பர்","parts":[{"text":"பொதும்பர்","lemma":"பொதும்பர்","gloss":"grove"}],"gloss":"grove"},{"surface":"நாண்மலர்","parts":[{"text":"நாண்மலர்","lemma":"நாண்மலர்","gloss":"fresh flower"}],"gloss":"fresh flower"},{"surface":"மயக்கி","parts":[{"text":"மயக்கு","lemma":"மயக்கு","gloss":"confuse"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having scattered"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விலங்கு","parts":[{"text":"விலங்கு","lemma":"விலங்கு","gloss":"obstructing"}],"gloss":"rising across"},{"surface":"திரை","parts":[{"text":"திரை","lemma":"திரை","gloss":"wave"}],"gloss":"wave"},{"surface":"உடைதரும்","parts":[{"text":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"break"},{"text":"தரும்","lemma":"தரு","gloss":"auxiliary verb"}],"gloss":"breaking"},{"surface":"துறைவனொ","parts":[{"text":"துறைவன்","lemma":"துறைவன்","gloss":"lord of the shore"},{"text":"ஒ","lemma":"ஒ","gloss":"with (part 1)"}],"gloss":"lord of the shore with"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"டிலங்கெயிறு","parts":[{"text":"டிலங்கெயிறு","lemma":"டிலங்கெயிறு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தோன்ற","parts":[{"text":"தோன்ற","lemma":"தோன்ற","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நக்கதன்","parts":[{"text":"நக்கதன்","lemma":"நக்கதன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பயனே","parts":[{"text":"பயனே","lemma":"பயனே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Ancient beauty having lost, beauty of shoulders having wasted away, / with a distressed heart, even at night without sleeping, / becoming pale, is it to perish? / Where white herons cry, in the cool fragrant seashore grove, / in the flower-rich grove, confusing the fresh flowers, / the lord of the shore where waves rise across and break, / with him, so that bright teeth appear, having laughed, is this the benefit?","translation":"Is this the only reward for having smiled at him, showing my bright teeth—that my ancient beauty is lost, my shoulders have wasted away, and with a distressed heart, I lie awake all night, perishing of pallor? He is the lord of the cool, fragrant seashore grove where white herons cry, and where waves rise across and break, scattering the fresh flowers in the flower-rich groves.","modern":"வெள்ளை நாரைகள் ஒலிக்கும் குளிர்ந்த மணமுள்ள கடற்கரைச் சோலையில், மலர்கள் நிறைந்த புதர்களில் உள்ள அன்றைய புதிய மலர்களைக் கலைத்து, குறுக்கே எழும் அலைகள் கரையில் வந்து உடையும் துறைமுகத் தலைவனுடன், என்னுடைய விளங்கும் பற்கள் தெரியும்படி நான் மகிழ்ந்து சிரித்ததன் பயன் இதுதானோ? என் பழமையான அழகு அழிந்து, தோள்களின் அழகு மெலிந்து, துன்பப்படும் நெஞ்சத்தோடு இரவிலும் தூங்காமல், பசலை நோய் கொண்டு நான் அழிய வேண்டுமா?","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the heroine's friend (தோழி) to the heroine, expressing deep concern over her deteriorating health due to her secret love affair with the lord of the maritime tract (neytal). The heroine has lost her natural beauty, her shoulders have become thin, and she is unable to sleep at night, consumed by the spreading pallor (பசலை) of separation. The friend questions whether this suffering is the only \"benefit\" of the happy moments they shared when she smiled at him. The imagery of the waves breaking violently and scattering the fresh flowers in the grove symbolizes how the hero's casual or delayed love is disrupting and destroying the heroine's delicate life. Key words like 'பசலை' (pallor), 'துறைவன்' (lord of the shore), and 'துஞ்சாது' (without sleeping) highlight the classic themes of the neytal landscape, which represents anxious waiting and despair.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}